The \emph{BV dual} (Barbasch--Vogan /
Lusztig) $\check{\mathcal{O}}$ is a partition subject to parity conditions:

\begin{center}
\begin{tabular}{c|l|l}
  $\star$ & Group & Dual partition $\check{\mathcal{O}}$ \\\hline
  $B$ & $\mathrm{SO}(2n+1)$ & all parts even, positive \\
  $D$ & $\mathrm{SO}(2n)$   & all parts odd \\
  $C$ & $\mathrm{Sp}(2n)$   & all parts odd \\
  $M = \tilde{C}$ & $\mathrm{Mp}(2n)$ & all parts even, positive \\
\end{tabular}
\end{center}

Composite D $\xrightarrow{
abla_{DC}}$ C $\xrightarrow{
abla_{CD}}$ D. After simplification: \[ (
abla^2_D 	au).\mathcal{P}(i, j) =  egin{cases}  ullet & i < 	au.\mathcal{Q}.\mathrm{colLen}(j + 1) \ s & 	au.\mathcal{Q}.\mathrm{colLen}(j + 1) \leq i < \mathrm{dotScolLen}(	au.\mathcal{P}, j + 1) \ 	au.\mathcal{P}(i, j + 1) & i \geq \mathrm{dotScolLen}(	au.\mathcal{P}, j + 1) \end{cases} \] (The resulting $\mathcal{Q}$ is all $ ullet$.)

Composite B $\xrightarrow{
abla_{BM}}$ M $\xrightarrow{
abla_{MB}}$ B.  egin{align*} (
abla^2_B 	au).\mathcal{P}(i, j) &=  egin{cases}  ullet & i < \mathrm{dotScolLen}(	au.\mathcal{P}, j + 1) \ 	au.\mathcal{P}(i, j + 1) & i \geq \ldots \end{cases} \ (
abla^2_B 	au).\mathcal{Q}(i, j) &=  egin{cases}  ullet & i < \mathrm{dotScolLen}(	au.\mathcal{P}, j + 1) \ s & \mathrm{dotScolLen}(	au.\mathcal{P}, j + 1) \leq i < \mathrm{dotScolLen}(	au.\mathcal{Q}, j + 1) \ 	au.\mathcal{Q}(i, j + 1) & i \geq \ldots \end{cases} \end{align*}

(Primitive case $\mathbf{r}_2(\check{\mathcal{O}}) > \mathbf{r}_3(\check{\mathcal{O}})$.) The signature splits as \[ \Sign(	au) = (\mathbf{c}_2(\mathcal{O}), \mathbf{c}_2(\mathcal{O})) + \Sign(
abla^2	au) + \mathrm{tailSig}(	au). \] More explicitly (Lean form):  egin{align*} p_	au &= \mathbf{c}_2(\mathcal{O}) + p_{
abla^2	au} + p_{	au_t} \ q_	au &= \mathbf{c}_2(\mathcal{O}) + q_{
abla^2	au} + q_{	au_t} \end{align*} where $\mathbf{c}_2(\mathcal{O}) = 	au.\mathcal{Q}.\mathrm{colLen}(0)$.

\textbf{Step 1 — unfold sign and fcSign of $E_{\mathrm{inner}}$.}
  $T^\gamma$ preserves both sign and fcSign (Lem~\ref{lem:twist_sign}, \ref{lem:twist_fcSign}), so we may work with $F := E \oplus (n_0, n_0) = (n_0, n_0) :: E$.
  By Lem~\ref{lem:augment_sign} (for $n_0 \geq 0$):
  \begin{align*}
    \Sign(F) &= (n_0 + \Sign(E).1 + \mathrm{fcSign}(E).2,\ n_0 + \Sign(E).2 + \mathrm{fcSign}(E).1). \\
    \mathrm{fcSign}(F) &= (n_0 + \mathrm{fcSign}(E).2,\ n_0 + \mathrm{fcSign}(E).1)
  \end{align*}
  using the cons formula for fcSign (the swap is due to parity index shift, Eq.~(9.12)).

  Substituting $\mathrm{fcSign}(E) = (\Sign(E).1 - n_{\mathrm{prev}},\ \Sign(E).2 - n_{\mathrm{prev}})$:
  \begin{align*}
    \Sign(F).1 &= n_0 + \Sign(E).1 + \Sign(E).2 - n_{\mathrm{prev}} = n_{\mathrm{inner}} \\
    \mathrm{fcSign}(F).2 &= n_0 + \Sign(E).1 - n_{\mathrm{prev}} = n_{\mathrm{inner}} - \Sign(E).2.
  \end{align*}

\textbf{Step 2 — substitute into the outer augment formula.}
  $p_\tau - \Sign(F).1 - \mathrm{fcSign}(F).2 = p_\tau - n_{\mathrm{inner}} - (n_{\mathrm{inner}} - \Sign(E).2) = p_\tau - 2 n_{\mathrm{inner}} + \Sign(E).2 = p_t$ (by hypothesis).

  The $q$-equation is symmetric.
